No third-party model weights are included
-----------------------------------------

This application reads a Samsung-paired Ōura Ring over Bluetooth LE and derives sleep, stress,
readiness and step figures from the raw frames. Doing that involves models and constants that are
Ōura Health Oy's, not ours.

**None of that material is in this repository, in any form.** Specifically, it carries no trained
model weights, no baked model constants, no decompiled vendor source, and no documentation
describing how to obtain any of it. The code that *reads* those models is ours and is published;
the payload it reads is not, and is fetched at runtime from private object storage by the deployment
that owns a licence to it. A clone of this repository will therefore start, build and pass its test
suite, and its Ōura-derived health figures will be unavailable until such a source is configured —
see `lib/oura-models/constants-delivery.ts` and `instrumentation-node.ts`, which fail the boot in
production rather than serving a degraded result quietly.

The test suite runs against synthetic constants generated by `scripts/generate-test-constants.js`:
every key preserved, every number replaced. They exercise the pipeline, and they are not the
vendor's values — do not read a passing test as evidence that any constant is correct.

`scripts/private-paths.json` is the machine-readable list of what must never appear here, and
`scripts/check-private-paths.js` enforces it on every pull request.

